# {{PROJECT}}

Entry point for humans and agents. Each layer below has one job; start at the
top and open only what the current phase needs.

## Start here

1. Read `galadon.yaml` for checks, deploy settings and artifact paths.
2. Run `galadon next`; do only the current phase.
3. Run `galadon check` before `galadon ship`.

## Where things live

| Layer | Path | Holds | Committed |
|---|---|---|---|
| Entry | `AGENTS.md`, `README.md` | the index into every layer | yes |
| Plan | `openspec/{config.yaml,changes/,specs/}` | construction tickets | yes |
| Truth | `spec/` | product behaviour facts | yes |
| Knowledge | `wiki/{knowledge,progress,runbook}/` | durable why, current state, operations | yes |
| Context | `.agents/{plans,wiki,evidence,skills,tmp,archive}/` | agent runtime state | no |
| Code | `server/`, `web/` | backend and frontend | yes |
| Run | `scripts/`, `deploy/`, `config.md` | scripts, deploy and environment | yes |
| Verify | `tests/`, `e2e/` | unit and end-to-end tests | yes |
| Output | `out/` | build output | no |

## Knowledge ownership

Project knowledge lives in `docs/` and `wiki/`; agent runtime state lives in
`.agents/` and is never committed; reusable cross-project knowledge lives in a
knowledge hub outside the repo — never keep a second copy here.

